<!--
  The app's mark for use inside the app, as the welcome screen shows it: the launcher artwork with
  its disc, and no tile.

  Same source as ic_launcher_foreground.xml — assets/icon_mk6.svg — and the same two things stripped
  from it, for the same reasons; read that file's comment first. The difference is the framing.

  WHY THIS EXISTS AT ALL. AboutScreen looked at putting the launcher icon on a page and used the
  wordmark instead, because the mk5 artwork is transparent, its ink runs from near-black to
  near-white, and every contrast ratio it was drawn to assumes the tile underneath it. Bare on a
  themed page it lost a different edge on each theme: the lower #3F3839 edges dissolve on the dark
  page at 1.1:1, the #F6E9E9 paper's outer edge dissolves on the light one at 1.05:1. That is the
  problem mk6's disc solves, and it solves it without a tile — so this is the same icon on both
  themes, carrying its own ground, with nothing square about it.

  NO GROUP TRANSFORM, unlike the launcher foreground. There is no mask here and no bleed, so the
  canvas is the drawing: the viewport is the source's own 779 units and the composable picks the
  size. At the welcome screen's 84dp the disc is 64.6dp across.

  The notebook is wider than the disc and overhangs it left and right. That is the source's own
  proportion, not a fault of the conversion — the book rests on the disc rather than sitting inside
  it.
-->
